```php
function smart_sort_array($set, $order = 'ASC') {
    // Check if set is an array
    if (!is_array($set)) {
        trigger_error('$set must be an array.', E_USER_ERROR);
    }

    // Loop through the array and sort elements based on age
    for ($i = 0; $i < count($set) - 1; $i++) {
        for ($j = $i + 1; $j < count($set); $j++) {
            if (($order === 'ASC' && $set[$i]['age'] > $set[$j]['age']) || ($order === 'DESC' && $set[$i]['age'] < $set[$j]['age'])) {
                // Swap elements
                $temp = $set[$i];
                $set[$i] = $set[$j];
                $set[$j] = $temp;
            }
        }
    }

    return $set;
}
```

This function accepts an associative array `$set` as its first argument and an optional second argument `$order`, which defaults to ascending order ('ASC'). It uses a nested loop to compare adjacent elements in the array based on their ages, and swaps them accordingly to achieve the desired sorting order.

