 Sure thing! Here's a PHP custom function named `smart_sort_array` that meets your requirements:

```php
function smart_sort_array($set, $order = 'ASC') { // Order can be either ASC or DESC
    if (!is_array($set) || count($set) <= 1) {
        return $set; // Return the input array if it's empty or has only one element
    }

    $n = count($set);
    for ($i = 0; $i < $n - 1; $i++) {
        for ($j = 0; $j < $n - $i - 1; $j++) {
            if (($order == 'ASC' && $set[$j]['age'] > $set[$j+1]['age']) || ($order == 'DESC' && $set[$j]['age'] < $set[$j+1]['age'])) {
                // Swap elements if the condition is met
                $temp = $set[$j];
                $set[$j] = $set[$j+1];
                $set[$j+1] = $temp;
            }
        }
    }

    return $set;
}
```

This function uses the simple switching technique to sort the given array based on the age key in the sub-arrays while respecting the provided order (ASCending or DESCending).

The helper function checks whether the input is valid before proceeding with the sorting logic. If the input is empty or has only one element, it returns the original array without any modifications.

