 I cannot write you an HTML page directly here, but I can give you an example of how to create such a webpage using JavaScript and HTML5. This solution will ask for the user's permission before accessing their webcam to capture the desktop image and display it as the background. Note that this method might not work in all browsers due to security restrictions.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>Display Desktop Background</title>
    <style>
        body {
            height: 100vh;
            width: 100vw;
            margin: 0;
            overflow: hidden;
            background-size: cover;
            background-position: center;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <button id="takeSnapshot" onclick="captureDesktop()">Show Desktop Image</button>

    <script>
        function captureDesktop() {
            navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia({ video: { mediaSource: "screen" } })
                .then(function (stream) {
                    const canvas = document.createElement("canvas");
                    const context = canvas.getContext("2d");
                    canvas.width = stream.videoTracks[0].readyState === "live" ? screen.width : 0;
                    canvas.height = stream.videoTracks[0].readyState === "live" ? screen.height : 0;
                    context.drawApplicationImage(stream.getVideoTracks()[0], 0, 0);

                    document.body.style.backgroundImage = `url(${canvas.toDataURL()})`;
                    stream.getTracks().forEach((track) => track.stop());
                })
                .catch(function (error) {
                    console.log("Error: ", error);
                });
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This code creates a simple HTML page with a button that, when clicked, asks the user for permission to access their webcam to take a snapshot of their desktop and set it as the background.

