 To use `react-native-fbsdk-next` in your JavaScript code and pass Facebook credentials, you need to set up the Facebook SDK with App ID and App Secret first. Here's a step-by-step guide:

1. Create a new Facebook App:
   Go to https://developers.facebook.com/apps and create a new app if you don't have one already. After creating an app, navigate to "Settings" > "Basic" tab and note down the `App ID`.

2. Add Platform:
   In the left sidebar, click on "Platforms" and add a new platform for your React Native app by selecting "React Native". Enter your bundle identifier (for iOS) or package name (for Android). Save changes.

3. Get App Secret:
   Go back to the "Settings" tab and scroll down to the "App Secrets" section. Click on "Add New App Secret". Copy the generated App Secret as it will not be shown again. Keep this secret safe!

4. Install `react-native-fbsdk-next`:
   Run the following command in your terminal to install the library:
   ```
   npm install react-native-fbsdk-next
   ```
5. Initialize Facebook SDK:
   Import the library in your entry file (index.js or main.js) and initialize it using your App ID:
   ```javascript
   import { LoginManager } from 'react-native-fbsdk';
   LoginManager.setLogInBehavior('web'); // This is optional but recommended for development
   LoginManager.logInWithPermissions(['public_profile', 'email']).then(
     function(result) {
       if (result.isCancelled) {
         console.log("Login cancelled");
       } else {
         AccessToken.fetchAccessTokenInfo().then((data) => {
           console.log(data);
         });
       }
     },
     function(error) {
       console.log("Login fail with error: " + error);
     }
   );
   ```
Replace `['public_profile', 'email']` with the required permissions for your use case.

Now, your `react-native-fbsdk-next` is initialized and ready to use with your App ID

 To use `react-native-fbsdk-next` in your JavaScript code with Facebook credentials, follow these steps:

